* sample.a0 -- a 6800 program for as0, the 6800/6802 cross-assembler.** It is here so that `as0' can be shown doing its job rather than printing* its usage line.  Assemble it with:   as0 /dd/DOC/xasm/sample.a0 - l s* and the S-record object lands in sample.a0.S19 in your data directory.*        org     $0100start   ldaa    #$41            load an 'A'        staa    $8000           write it to the port        ldab    count        decb        stab    count        bne     start        swicount   fcb     $05msg     fcc     "6800"        end